---
import { DEMO_URL, DEPLOY_URL } from "../../site";
---
<section class="section" id="plans" aria-labelledby="plans-title">
  <div class="head">
    <p class="eyebrow">Plans</p>
    <h2 id="plans-title">One price per company. No seats.</h2>
    <p>Start free with the open source core. Each paid plan has one yearly price per company. The number of people does not change the price. Nonprofits get 50% off every paid plan.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="bento">
    <article class="card plan s4">
      <p class="eyebrow">For everyone</p>
      <h3>Free</h3>
      <p class="per">Open source, Apache License 2.0</p>
      <ul>
        <li>The core, the UI and Projects</li>
        <li>Agent with approvals</li>
        <li>Bring your own AI</li>
        <li>Many companies, no seat limits</li>
        <li>Your own Cloudflare account</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={DEPLOY_URL}>Deploy to Cloudflare</a>
    </article>
    <article class="card plan featured s4">
      <span class="chip ok tagline">Free on the demo</span>
      <p class="eyebrow">Growing organizations</p>
      <h3>Director</h3>
      <p class="per">Yearly, one price per company</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Everything in Free</li>
        <li>Docs: live editing and comments</li>
        <li>Advisory: a marketplace with Stripe</li>
        <li>New paid apps as they join</li>
        <li>Stripe on a hosted site, or a license key</li>
        <li>50% off for nonprofits</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="btn btn-accent" href={DEMO_URL}>Try Director on the demo</a>
    </article>
    <article class="card plan s4">
      <p class="eyebrow warm">Custom Apps as a Service</p>
      <h3>Producer</h3>
      <p class="per">Yearly, one price per company</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Everything in Director</li>
        <li>Done for you: we install and manage OpenAct</li>
        <li>We work with you to build your primary custom app</li>
        <li>50% off for nonprofits</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://docs.openact.ing/plans">Read about Producer</a>
    </article>
    <div class="card q s6"><h3>How is the price set?</h3><p>Each paid plan has one yearly price per company. Choose Director to build your own apps. Choose Producer when you want us to do the work. Nonprofits pay half.</p></div>
    <div class="card q s6"><h3>How do I pay?</h3><p>On a hosted OpenAct site, a company owner pays on the Plan page with Stripe. On your own deploy, MarketGrowth gives you a license key.</p></div>
    <div class="card q s6"><h3>What happens without a plan?</h3><p>On a hosted site, the paid apps lock, but their data stays. They come back with all their data when the plan comes back. On your own deploy, the app versions you have keep working when your license ends. You renew to get updates and new apps.</p></div>
    <div class="card q s6"><h3>Can I try the paid apps first?</h3><p>Yes. The demo has Docs and Advisory on for every company. The demo deletes all data every night.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
